vendor/pl_mpeg: two fixes to pl_mpeg.h (c871f2b) that no upstream commit has.

1. The declaration half uses FILE * (plm_create_with_file, plm_buffer_create_with_file) but only
   the implementation half includes <stdio.h>, since upstream PR #56 (PLM_NO_STDIO): as shipped
   the header does not compile ("unknown type name 'FILE'"). <stddef.h> and, unless
   PLM_NO_STDIO, <stdio.h> are included where the declarations start.
2. There is no export macro, so a Windows DLL exports nothing. PLM_API -- empty unless defined,
   __declspec(dllexport) for fetch.toml's DLL entry -- now opens each of the 87 public
   declarations. It changes nothing in the static build or the translation.

Made by RFC-0005 P0 (claude-docs docs/tiko-vendor/probes/av0) with an awk one-liner over the
declaration half. Worth offering upstream.

